# --- bind/ : native dependencies ---
# Most of bind/windows/ is ALREADY TRACKED (the mscrt/ucrt/icu runtime DLLs and
# the debug DLLs, 51 files ~8 MB). gitignore does not untrack existing files, so
# those stay committed regardless of the rules below - which is what the Windows
# release build needs, since windows/CMakeLists.txt installs them into the bundle.
#
# bind/windows/core/sing-box.exe is a custom patched build (version metadata
# stripped, endpoint patch applied) and CANNOT be replaced with a stock upstream
# release, so it is committed too - CI needs it in the checkout.
#
# Only the large platform cores we do not build on Windows runners stay ignored.
# NOTE: exclude '/bind/*' then re-include, NOT '/bind/'. Git cannot re-include a
# file if a PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, which makes every '!' rule dead.
/bind/*
!/bind/windows/
/bind/windows/core/*.bak-before-endpoint
/bind/windows/core/*.bak
/bind/android/
/bind/linux/
/bind/apple/
# --- build / session junk (not source) ---
.flutter_tool_state
cache.db
tags.txt
.github/context-mode/sessions/
*.bak-oom
*.bak-before-endpoint
notary_log.json

# --- signing material: NEVER commit ---
# Android release/debug keystores and their passwords. Losing control of the
# release key means anyone can sign an APK that Android accepts as an official
# update to this app, and Android signing keys cannot be revoked or rotated
# once published. CI must read these from GitHub Secrets instead.
android/key.properties
android/sign/
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
